/*
 * Custom icon path data for the side panel.
 *
 * SPDX-License-Identifier: CC0-1.0
 *
 * (Card 72: this used to read `Apache-2.0`, for the Material Symbols glyphs
 * that filled this file before card 66 replaced them with Hugeicons. Not one
 * of those paths survives, so the identifier now covers what's actually
 * here — the CC0 Ollama trace described below, alongside the `sparkle` mark
 * drawn for this project.)
 *
 * Card 66 (decisions/28-shadcn-svelte-maia-zinc.md) moved every standard
 * glyph to Hugeicons (`@hugeicons/core-free-icons`, mapped by name inside
 * Icon.svelte). This file now only carries the two marks that AREN'T a
 * stock Hugeicons glyph:
 *
 * `sparkle` is ours — a plain symmetric four-point star. Chrome's Gemini
 * panel uses Google's own product mark there, which is a trademark and not
 * something to copy.
 *
 * `ollama` is the real Ollama logo — Simple Icons' CC0-licensed trace
 * (https://simpleicons.org/?q=ollama,
 * https://github.com/simple-icons/simple-icons/blob/develop/icons/ollama.svg),
 * mechanically rescaled from their 24x24 grid onto this file's 960-unit one
 * (`scale(40, 40).translate(0, -960)`, via the `svgpath` package) — no path
 * data was hand-edited.
 *
 * Both paths share the same 960-unit grid, so Icon.svelte renders them at
 * viewBox="0 -960 960 960" and no path needs re-normalising to a 24x24 box.
 */

